problem:
Problem description
- There is a weekly production planning problem with a set of products $$\mathcal{P}$$ indexed by $$p$$ and a set of resources $$\mathcal{R}$$ indexed by $$r$$.
- Each product $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ has a unit resource usage profile, a unit selling price $$s_p$$, a unit variable production cost $$c_p$$, and an associated special equipment with weekly fixed cost $$f_p$$.
- Each resource $$r \in \mathcal{R}$$ has a weekly availability limit $$b_r$$.
- A demand parameter $$d_p$$ may be included as an optional upper bound on how many units of product $$p$$ can be sold, but no explicit demand cap is required in this problem instance.
- The factory decides how many units of each product to produce during the week and whether to activate the corresponding special equipment.
- Production of any product is allowed only when its corresponding special equipment is activated for the week.
- The total use of each resource by all produced products must remain within the available weekly capacity of that resource.
- The planning goal is to maximize total weekly profit, defined as total sales revenue minus total variable production costs minus total fixed equipment costs.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_p$$: the weekly production quantity of product $$p$$, where $$x_p \ge 0$$.
  - $$y_p$$: a binary activation variable for the special equipment of product $$p$$, where $$y_p = 1$$ means the equipment is used in the week and $$y_p = 0$$ means it is not used.
  - $$\Pi$$: the resulting total weekly profit.

Input Format
{
  "sets": {
    "products": {
      "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{P}$$",
      "description": "Set of products, indexed by $$p$$."
    },
    "resources": {
      "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{R}$$",
      "description": "Set of resources, indexed by $$r$$."
    },
    "time_horizon": {
      "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
      "description": "Planning periods, indexed by $$t$$; this problem uses a weekly planning horizon."
    }
  },
  "parameters": {
    "resource_usage": {
      "symbol": "$$a_{r,p}$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}| \\times |\\mathcal{P}|$$",
      "description": "Units of resource $$r$$ required to produce one unit of product $$p$$."
    },
    "selling_price": {
      "symbol": "$$s_p$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}|$$",
      "description": "Unit selling price of product $$p$$."
    },
    "variable_cost": {
      "symbol": "$$c_p$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}|$$",
      "description": "Unit variable production cost of product $$p$$."
    },
    "fixed_cost": {
      "symbol": "$$f_p$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}|$$",
      "description": "Weekly fixed cost for activating the special equipment used to produce product $$p$$."
    },
    "resource_capacity": {
      "symbol": "$$b_r$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}|$$",
      "description": "Weekly available capacity of resource $$r$$."
    },
    "demand_cap": {
      "symbol": "$$d_p$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}|$$",
      "description": "Optional maximum weekly sellable demand for product $$p$$; if omitted, demand is assumed not to bind."
    }
  },
  "assumptions": {
    "equipment_product_link": "Each product $$p$$ has one dedicated special equipment.",
    "sales_assumption": "All produced units are sold within the week at the stated selling price."
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "solution": {
    "production_quantity": {
      "symbol": "$$x_p$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}|$$",
      "description": "Weekly production quantity for each product $$p$$."
    },
    "equipment_activation": {
      "symbol": "$$y_p$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{P}|$$",
      "description": "Binary activation decision for the special equipment of each product $$p$$."
    },
    "total_profit": {
      "symbol": "$$\\Pi$$",
      "description": "Maximum achievable weekly profit."
    }
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "sets": {
    "products": ["shirt", "short_sleeve", "casual_cloth"],
    "resources": ["labor", "material"],
    "time_horizon": ["week"]
  },
  "parameters": {
    "resource_usage": [
      [3, 2, 6],
      [4, 3, 6]
    ],
    "selling_price": [120, 80, 180],
    "variable_cost": [60, 40, 80],
    "fixed_cost": [2000, 1500, 1000],
    "resource_capacity": [1500, 1600]
  }
}
